{
  "explanation": "Hi Meera, you are doing a fantastic job staying curious about the world around you! The sky looks blue because of how sunlight interacts with gases in Earth's atmosphere, a process called Rayleigh scattering. Sunlight contains all the colors of the rainbow. Blue light travels in smaller, shorter waves than the other colors, so it gets scattered in every direction much more than the other colors when it hits the air molecules. When you look up, you see all that scattered blue light!",
  "practice_question": "What is the name of the scientific process that causes the sky to appear blue by scattering shorter light waves?"
}

